+# Implementation Plan: JSON Pointer Resolution (RFC 6901)
+
+**Spec**: [spec.md](spec.md) | **Branch**: 001-json-pointer-resolve
+
+## Technical Context
+- Language: TypeScript (strict, NodeNext), no runtime dependencies (README).
+- Tests: `node --test` (Node 22, built-in type stripping), test files in `test/*.test.ts`.
+- Single module `src/pointer.ts` re-exported from `src/index.ts` (later features will import it).
+- No NEEDS CLARIFICATION remain.
+
+## Constitution Check
+`.specify/memory/constitution.md` is still the unfilled template: no ratified rules, so no gates. README rule applied: follow the published standard; no runtime dependency.
+
+## Design
+Parse the pointer (validate leading `/`, `~` escapes) into tokens, then walk the document: arrays need canonical index tokens in range; objects use own-property check (`Object.hasOwn`); anything else throws. Errors are plain `Error`.
+
+See [research.md](research.md), [data-model.md](data-model.md), [contracts/api.md](contracts/api.md), [quickstart.md](quickstart.md).
